    "steps": [
      "Blend all the paste ingredients into a rough purée. Wear gloves when handling the scotch bonnets.",
      "Rub the paste well into the chicken, getting it into the slashes. Cover and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 6 hours, ideally overnight.",
      "For the oven, heat to 200°C, place the chicken on a rack over a tray and roast for 45 to 55 minutes, turning once, until the juices run clear (74°C at the thickest point). For a grill, cook over indirect medium heat with the lid closed for 40 to 50 minutes, adding pimento wood or wood chips for smoke, then finish over direct heat for the last few minutes to char.",
